\title{Universal Property of the Subspace Topology}
\taxon{Proposition}
\import{macros}
\p{
    Let #{A\subseteq X} carry the [subspace topology](def-000D), and let
    #{\iota:A\hookrightarrow X} be the inclusion. A map #{f:Z\to A} is
    continuous if and only if #{\iota\circ f:Z\to X} is continuous.
}
\proof{
    The inclusion is continuous: for every open #{U\subseteq X}, its preimage
    is #{A\cap U}, which is open in #{A}. Thus the forward implication follows
    from [closure under composition](thm-001D).

    Conversely, suppose #{\iota\circ f} is continuous. Every open subset of
    #{A} has the form #{A\cap U} for some open #{U\subseteq X}, and
    ##{
        f^{-1}(A\cap U)=(\iota\circ f)^{-1}(U).
    }
    This set is open in #{Z}, so #{f} is continuous.
}
